Q: How to select a dropdown built as a button (Selenium/Python) A: <p>Generally the dropdown menus are <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> tags. However the modern day <a href="https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tag_select.asp" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Bootstrap Dropdown</a> can be rendered using <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;li&gt;</code>. As an example:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;ul class=&quot;dropdown-menu&quot;&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;HTML&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;CSS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;JavaScript&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</code></pre>
<hr />
<h2>This usecase</h2>
<p>Similarly the HTML you provided:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;SLP-dropdown SLP-dropdown-placement-bottomLeft&quot; data-qa=&quot;SLP-dropdown&quot; style=&quot;left: 429px; top: 436px; width: 117px;&quot;&gt;
    &lt;ul class=&quot;SLP-dropdown-menu SLP-dropdown-menu-root SLP-dropdown-menu-vertical&quot; role-“menu&quot; tabindex=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
        &lt;li class=&quot;SLP-dropdown-menu-item&quot; role=&quot;menuitem&quot;&gt;Choice 1&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li class=&quot;SLP-dropdown-menu-item&quot; role=&quot;menuitem&quot;&gt;Choice 2&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li class=&quot;SLP-dropdown-menu-item&quot; role=&quot;menuitem&quot;&gt;Choice 3&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li class=&quot;SLP-dropdown-menu-item&quot; role=&quot;menuitem&quot;&gt;Choice 4&lt;/li&gt;

</code></pre>
<p>is also a <em>Bootstrap Dropdown</em></p>
<hr />
<h2>Solution</h2>
<p>To select the option with text as <strong>Choice 4</strong>, you have to induce <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/49775502/webdriverwait-not-working-as-expected/49775808#49775808">WebDriverWait</a> for the desired <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/72134009/7429447"><em><code>element_to_be_clickable()</code></em></a> and you can use the following <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/48369043/official-locator-strategies-for-the-webdriver">locator strategies</a>:</p>
<pre><code>import selenium
from selenium import webdriver

from selenium.webdriver.support.ui import WebDriverWait
from selenium.webdriver.support import expected_conditions as EC
from selenium.webdriver.common.by import By

driver = webdriver.Chrome()
driver.get(&quot;https://sample URL&quot;)
WebDriverWait(driver, 20).until(EC.element_to_be_clickable((By.XPATH, &quot;//ul[@class='SLP-dropdown-menu SLP-dropdown-menu-root SLP-dropdown-menu-vertical']&quot;))).click()
WebDriverWait(driver, 20).until(EC.element_to_be_clickable((By.XPATH, &quot;//li[text()='Choice 4']&quot;))).click()
</code></pre>
